## Attempt 1 — config-tier stop (same class as codex-cli's attempt 1)

```
node p012-live-proof.mjs coord_p012_live_76518_glm glm-cli full
```
Transcript: `glm-cli-attempt1-config-tier-stop.stdout.log` / `.stderr.log`.

```
RunnerConfigError: no model configured for policy tier "standard" under provider "z-ai".
```
`.fgos/config.json`'s `glm-cli` entry declares `providerModel: "z-ai"` and a
`rigorOverrides` table (`light/standard/heavy -> lightweight`), but
`resolveAssignmentDispatchPolicy`'s direct `resolvePolicyTierModel(cfg,
effectiveTier, resolvedProvider)` call (traced in
`src/runner/dispatch/assignment-policy.mjs`, unmodified by this cell) does
not consult `rigorOverrides` before that lookup -- `modelPolicies.z-ai` only
declares `lightweight`, not `standard` (this repo's default tier absent an
override). Same shape as codex-cli's attempt 1; same worked-around fix:
`cliOverride.model` short-circuits the tier lookup entirely.

## Attempt 2 — genuine live timeout (real subprocess, real 180s bound, honest failure)

```
node p012-live-proof.mjs coord_p012_live_76518_glm glm-cli resume z-ai/glm-5.2
```
Transcript: `glm-cli-attempt2-timeout.stdout.log` / `.stderr.log`.

`dispatch-plan.json`/RunResult `policy` confirm accurate provenance BEFORE
the hang: `executorId: "glm-cli"`, `provenance.provider.value: "z-ai"`,
`provenance.model.value: "z-ai/glm-5.2"` (source `cliOverride`),
`governance.value: "allowed"`, `source.id: "z-ai"` -- config and governance
were both correct; this is not an "absent/unconfigured/wrong-tier/auth"
failure. The real `claude` subprocess (glm-cli routes through the `claude`
CLI binary with `ANTHROPIC_*` env overridden to OpenRouter's GLM 5.2 model,
per `.fgos/config.json`'s own description) was genuinely spawned and hung
with no further output until the bound fired:
```
"status": "failed", "confidence": "failed"
"runtime": {"exitCode": 124, ...}
"agentClaim": {"status":"failed","summary":"executor timed out after 180000ms for work \"glm-cli\"."}
"evidence": {"gitBefore":"626e057b...","gitAfter":"626e057b...", "changedFiles":[]}
```
Exit code 124 (timeout), zero repository mutation (`gitBefore === gitAfter`).
This is the SAME live-executor timeout pattern P00.3 already documented and
disposed as a legitimate honest partial, not a stop gate ("a real timeout is
legitimate evidence, never faked away" -- P01.2's own Bug Taxonomy, quoting
that precedent). Per the Doer prompt's explicit instruction for this exact
scenario, this is recorded honestly and NOT retried further, since codex-cli
already produced one fully successful end-to-end proof (primary AND consult
both completing) -- the bar for `DONE_WITH_CONCERNS` rather than `BLOCKED`.

No secret value (API key, auth token) appears in either log file (checked
directly: `grep -n "AUTH_TOKEN=.\|API_KEY=."` on both -- no match; only the
env-var *names* the config declares, never a value, matching P00.3's own
secret-redaction discipline).

No repository mutation from either glm-cli attempt: `git status --porcelain`
before and after these two attempts is identical (modulo this proof
directory's own untracked files, which are proof output, not a side effect
of the live-proof script) and `git rev-parse HEAD` is unchanged
(`626e057b181510558e69064570c1cc4ed9794bd9`) throughout.
